Subject: [PATCH 05/26] Sync CameraXFrameSource frame pacing from Mosip26 (Part
 1)

CameraXFrameSource.java and engine-sync.txt from Mosip26 79567b1 ("Part 1:
CameraXFrameSource paces delivery to maxDeliverFps before converting"): the
source now delivers at most 15 fps by default (time-based, on the camera
timestamp, checked before any conversion; 10% jitter allowance), so a 30 fps
camera converts half the frames. On the S23 FE: camera 30 fps, delivered
15 fps, YUV conversion about 16% of one core during challenges (it was about
50%).

CameraXFrameSourcePacingTest (JVM): 30 fps with jitter -> 30 of 60 frames
delivered with sequence gaps of 2, no getPlanes() on skipped frames, every
image closed; stride alone; stride then pacing; 0 = unlimited; negative
rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
